# Project Workflow

- Inspect the current implementation before making changes.
- Work on one feature-sized change at a time.
- Preserve existing behavior and avoid unnecessary rewrites.
- After changes, run all practical checks such as lint and build.
- If a check fails, identify and fix the cause, then run the check again.
- After successful verification, briefly report the changed files and behavior.
- Do not commit or push before the feature works correctly.
- Commit or push only after the user confirms the feature works in the UI.
- Before starting the next feature, briefly explain what will be done.
- Use plain explanations. Give exact commands only when the user must run them.

# Report Style

- Preserve the previously provided Hyunsik intelligence-report standards for article titles, summaries, reports, and AI prompts.
- Treat the style guide as higher priority than generic Korean writing conventions.
- Do not make major changes to report style or AI prompts without first explaining the proposed change to the user.
